{
  "content_acceptable": false,
  "critical_error": true,
  "critical_evidence": [
    {
      "quote_or_cell": "Provisional release: for urgent program needs, the vendor can proceed at a provisional price, subject to a cap, while the final price is settled. This must be recorded and approved by the Program Manager and Purchase.",
      "why_wrong": "This creates an actionable exception allowing a vendor to proceed on changed commercial terms without Finance controller approval. The operative approved record requires Finance controllers, Program Managers and Purchase for price changes. The three-way approval statements elsewhere do not resolve this conflicting release instruction; the platform could implement it as a bypass.",
      "correction": "Require Finance controller, Program Manager and Purchase approval of the provisional price or capped commercial commitment before vendor authorization. Also make clear that provisional release cannot bypass applicable revised-TRSO, technical or quality gates. Final price settlement must follow the same mandatory commercial approval rule."
    }
  ],
  "omissions": [],
  "evaluation_defect": false,
  "defect_reason": "",
  "rationale": "The submission correctly resolves the conflicting approval sources using the approved, in-force record rather than the newer draft. It substantively covers modular quotation drivers, supplier evaluation, TRSO and nomination signoffs, delta-based change handling, version control, communication records and digital platform requirements. However, its provisional-release route contradicts the mandatory Finance approval requirement and requires substantive repair before the workflow can safely serve as a platform blueprint."
}
